+### Milestone 2026.07.475 (same-day addendum -- timing-integrity mismatch traced to a self-referential detector bug, not new experiment activity)
+- exp_range: no new experiment commits since the prior retro pass per `git log 958859613..HEAD` (exactly one subsequent commit, a docs-sync task, not an experiment); not derivable from the TIMING DATA block itself
+- theme: second retro pass for this milestone, triggered by a freshly-raised TIMING INTEGRITY MISMATCH flag; root-caused to the mismatch-detector's own logic rather than to genuinely missed experiment activity
+- key result: honest negative on new experiment commits (still 0), but the "mismatch" itself is very likely a false positive -- `scripts/research_conductor.py`'s check builds `milestone_marker = f"milestone {current}"` yet tests bare `current in changelog_text`, so it fires on the prior retro pass's own auto-appended changelog line (confirmed via grep: exactly one hit, that entry) rather than on genuine untracked experiment evidence; every retro pass is required to append a changelog line naming the milestone, so any milestone with 2+ retro passes will always trip this flag regardless of real activity. Supplementary `ops/conductor-log.md` read confirms no PHASE task attempts between the 10:35 UTC success and 11:43 UTC, only a failed 1201s Codex CLI "Plan next milestone" idle-timeout (the fourth such stall logged today)
+- acceptance: 0/0 criteria met -- no experiment criteria were present in the supplied timing data this pass; the detector root-cause is a supplementary operational diagnosis, not a milestone research deliverable
