 - 2026-07-03: Operational retrospective for milestone 2026.07.475 (✅ Complete) — TIMING DATA reports 0 completed experiments this pass (locked fields correctly stay at total_wall_time_minutes=0, experiments_completed=0, compute_bound_experiments_count=0, slowest_experiments=[], gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null), now independently confirmed by both live git-log and disk-mtime reconstruction rather than the previously-diagnosed FALSE-ZERO detector gap (.469/.472/.473x3/.474x4). Supplementary check of ops/conductor-log.md (outside the TIMING DATA block) found the real story: every queued .475 phase hit an identical self-heal pre-test failure ("1 failed, 116 passed, 15 warnings") for roughly an hour (08:42-09:42 UTC) until the conductor daemon restarted at 10:35:54 UTC, immediately followed by the first successful task registration at 10:35 UTC (via a "deliverable already exists" reuse, not a fresh clean self-heal pass) -- consistent with, and an apparent validation of, the .474 retro's restart recommendation, though not yet confirmed durable. estimated_time_savings_pct=30; results/operational_retro_2026_07_475.json
+- 2026-07-03: Operational retrospective for milestone 2026.07.475, second pass (✅ Complete) — this pass's supplied TIMING DATA flagged a new TIMING INTEGRITY MISMATCH (both live git-log and disk-mtime reconstruction found 0 experiment commits, yet ops/changelog.md contains entries referencing 2026.07.475). Investigation found this is very likely a false positive in the mismatch-detector itself rather than new untracked experiment activity: `git log 958859613..HEAD` shows exactly one subsequent commit (a docs-sync task, not an experiment), and `grep -n "2026\.07\.475" ops/changelog.md` returns exactly one hit -- the prior retro pass's own appended summary line (the entry immediately above this one). Root cause located by reading (not modifying) `scripts/research_conductor.py`'s mismatch check: it builds `milestone_marker = f"milestone {current}"` but then tests bare `current in changelog_text` instead of `milestone_marker in changelog_text`, so `milestone_marker` is dead code and the check trivially fires the moment the milestone number appears ANYWHERE in changelog.md -- including this task's own mandated changelog append, which every retro pass writes. Consequence: any milestone that receives a second-or-later retro pass will always trip this flag regardless of real activity, self-poisoning the very detector meant to catch the FALSE-ZERO class. Supplementary ops/conductor-log.md read: no PHASE/experiment attempts logged between the 10:35 UTC success (carried from the prior pass) and 11:43 UTC, a ~68-minute gap containing only a failed 1201s Codex CLI "Plan next milestone" idle-timeout -- the fourth such ~20-minute planner stall logged today (06:14, 07:05, 07:56, 11:43 UTC). estimated_time_savings_pct=15; results/operational_retro_2026_07_475.json
